# Architecture docs (living atlas)

## Before structural / product changes

Read the matching page(s) under `docs/architecture/` (hub: `docs/architecture/README.md`).

## Same-change updates required when touching

- Boundaries / topology → `00-system-overview.md` (+ affected page)
- `apps/api/Endpoints/*`, `Program.cs` → `02-api.md` (+ `00` if topology changes)
- `apps/api/Data/*`, `infra/migrations/*` → `03-data-model.md`
- `apps/api/Ingest/*` → `04-ingestion.md`
- `apps/admin/**` → `05-admin.md`
- `apps/app/**` → `06-reader-app.md`
- `packages/shared-types/**`, OpenAPI → `07-shared-types.md`
- `render.yaml`, docker, Cloudflare, env examples, CI deploy → `08-hosting-and-ci.md`
- Workspace layout / root scripts → `01-monorepo.md`

## Rules

1. Bump **Last verified against** on every edited atlas page.
2. New subsystem → page from `docs/architecture/_template.md`, link from hub README, add a row to this mapping.
3. No parallel “how it works now” docs outside `docs/architecture/`.
4. If atlas and code disagree, fix in the **same change** (prefer atlas → intended design; fix code if atlas was correct and code drifted).
5. Do not rewrite ADRs for current behavior — ADRs are decision history.
